The `openclaw` name that appears in file names, API paths and machine paths
(openclaw.json, /openclaw/... endpoints, patches/, SSH hosts) is the name of an
earlier framework. Those locations really carry that name on disk and on the
API, so the code and docs spell it as it is. The Blave Agent runtime in
runtime/ has been first-party since 2026-07-25 (see runtime/CHANGELOG.md) and
is unrelated to that product.

The desktop shell in shell/ launches — but does not redistribute — third-party
agent CLIs (Claude Code, Codex) that the user installs and authenticates
themselves. Electron, used by the shell at build time, is MIT licensed.
